# 8. Expensive car vs driver: productivity spending ka framework

Creator ka practical example:

Agar aap ₹20 lakh ki car afford kar sakte ho:

* ₹10–12 lakh ki car lo,
* remaining difference ka part driver par use karo.

Reason:

Driver potentially aapko time wapas deta hai.

Woh handle kar sakta hai:

* family pickups,
* hospital runs,
* relatives,
* errands,
* miscellaneous driving.

Aapka time free ho sakta hai:

* learning ke liye,
* side income,
* work,
* relaxation,
* family.

Creator ka spending test:

**“Kya yeh paisa vanity me ja raha hai, ya meri productivity/relaxation/time improve kar raha hai?”**



---

# 9. Sabse bada wealth goal: apne din ka ownership

Creator ka strongest career principle:

> **“I should own 2/3 of my day.”**

Uska breakdown roughly:

24 hours me sleeping/body maintenance ke baad ~16 usable hours hain.

Ideal state:

* ~10 hours apne control me,
* ~6 hours unavoidable obligations.

Woh provocative language me conventional employment ko “slavery” se compare karta hai, lekin simultaneously clarify karta hai ki **young people ko first few years job zaroor karni chahiye**.

Job sikhati hai:

* punctuality,
* discipline,
* communication,
* organisational structure,
* HR,
* sales,
* finance,
* teamwork,
* mentorship.

Goal job ko refuse karna nahi; **job ko permanent identity mat banao.**



---

# 10. “Apna kaam thakata hai, dusre ka kaam stress deta hai”

Creator ka memorable distinction:

**Apne kaam se fatigue aata hai.
Dusre ke control wale kaam se stress aata hai.**

Uske according ideal career trajectory:

1. job karo,
2. skills seekho,
3. apne liye time preserve karo,
4. reusable assets banao,
5. personal brand develop karo,
6. gradually income ko time-selling se detach karo.

Examples:

* potter pots bana kar inventory sell karta hai;
* author ek book likhkar repeatedly royalties earn kar sakta hai;
* course creator ek recorded course repeatedly sell kar sakta hai.

Point: **sirf hours sell karne ke bajaye effort ko reusable asset me convert karo.**



